1281 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 331 0 R
/T (This project provides a data-driven approach to automated product categorization by combining exploratory analysis, NLP-based feature engineering, machine learning classification, model evaluation, and explainability. The findings highlight how product naming patterns, technical specifications, character-level features, and category-specific terminology contribute to accurate classification across ten product categories. Model evaluation demonstrates the effectiveness of character-level TF-IDF and Ridge Classifier, achieving a Macro F1-score of 0.9886 on the test set, while identifying classification challenges involving closely related product categories and ambiguous product titles. The project establishes a foundation for improving product taxonomy management through enhanced text representations, ambiguity detection, classification confidence assessment, and further model optimization.)
/E (This project provides a data-driven approach to automated product categorization by combining exploratory analysis, NLP-based feature engineering, machine learning classification, model evaluation, and explainability. The findings highlight how product naming patterns, technical specifications, character-level features, and category-specific terminology contribute to accurate classification across ten product categories. Model evaluation demonstrates the effectiveness of character-level TF-IDF and Ridge Classifier, achieving a Macro F1-score of 0.9886 on the test set, while identifying classification challenges involving closely related product categories and ambiguous product titles. The project establishes a foundation for improving product taxonomy management through enhanced text representations, ambiguity detection, classification confidence assessment, and further model optimization.)
/Pg 71 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
